# The §22B-1e2a failing-first run

Command:

    tools/unity-identity-channel/scripts/run_channel_measurement.sh --expect-durable-join --runs 1

`--expect-durable-join` asserts the optimistic contract: that the identity a
candidate exports tells every definition of the measured document apart. The
document contains two imported sources that use the same source-local key
`step.product_definition#42`, so the current production property cannot.

The editor really imported all 48 vanilla scenarios first; this is the assertion
at the end of the run, on the real editor, not a stub:

```text
FCAD_CHANNEL_IDENTITY_FAILURE System.InvalidOperationException: the exported identity of a-control cannot tell two definitions apart: key:step.product_definition#42
```

The runner then refused the whole run:

```text
Unity exited 1
```

The same assertion passes for every candidate that carries `ImportedSourceId`
beside the source-local key. That is the measurement, and it is recorded in
`expected/channel-decision.json` rather than remembered.
